{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-116579",
  "enisaUuid": "58d465ca-5b2c-3245-b7bb-7a4254b75ea5",
  "description": "A vulnerability was found in miroslavpejic85 MiroTalk P2P up to 2.0.87/2.1.38. Affected by this issue is the function CheckPassword of the file app/src/server.js of the component Socket IO Handler. Performing a manipulation of the argument peer_id results in improper access controls. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. Upgrading to version 2.1.39 can resolve this issue. The patch is named 4e40471abc48bfc32b4b174b8844716dfc5c1471. You should upgrade the affected component.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 3, 2026, 10:30:15 PM",
